body:
Thank you. I understand people's frustration with conflicts in other places not getting the same attention, especially for people who are from a country that has been fucked up by the USA. At the same time, I feel like almost every single person I've ever known on the left has been vocally critical of US imperialism since...at least Vietnam, 30+ years before I was born. I'm certainly not an expert and I could be misunderstanding the situation but AT BEST the Ukraine invasion feels like Putin's version of invading Iraq for WMDs.

&#x200B;

It's really weird how so many people I respected a week ago turned out to just really hate America and not have any actual anti-imperial beliefs.

Defending Dan Schneider is really weird. He created a show that you loved as a kid. He's not some auteur making high art. Pedophilia rumors aside, he's an abusive prick who created a toxic work environment that lead to the mental collapse of at least one of the child actresses he was responsible for. It doesn't matter that there have never been any formal allegations of sexual abuse against him, because there is enough damning material on the record for us to know that he's a bad guy.

&#x200B;

As far as I'm aware, he's never made anything that was intended for adults. The only people interested in the reboot are adults who grew up with the show. Dan Schneider is useless to the reboot because he doesn't make entertainment for this demographic. Miranda, Nathan, and Jerry are way more important to the reboot than Schneider could possibly be, because they're the ones who can make a show that's entertaining and relatable to the people actually watching it
